<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Telecom, Telebras seek Argentina business.</title>
<headline>Portugal Telecom, Telebras seek Argentina business.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal Telecom and Brazil's Telebras will jointly bid for a licence to operate a third mobile phone network in Buenos Aires, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman was confirming a report in the 'Capital' newspaper which quoted Telecom chairman Francisco Murteira Nabo as saying the two companies, allied in the Alianca Atlantica, would make a joint bid.</p>
<p>According to Murteira Nabo, investment in the project would involve some $500 million over five years.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
